Documented here → [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4222812658/WIP+Looker+data+fetching+setup+for+provider+portal|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4222812658/WIP+Looker+data+fetching+setup+for+provider+portal|smart-link]





*Introduction*:- To Build a tool which will fetch data from Looker and cache it, so we can use it in the provider portal.

*Background*:- Looker queries are slow, so to display Looker data in the provider portal, we need to cache the data that we need. 

*Design Documents* :- [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4187783773/Design+Doc+Provider+Portal+Promotions+Page+UX+changs|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4187783773/Design+Doc+Provider+Portal+Promotions+Page+UX+changs|smart-link]

*Solution*:- We can setup a cron which will run every X hrs and run few looker queries. We have verified with Boris  and he has said that he will give us the query which will fetch data needed on all the pages in provider portal. (_Boris has mentioned that he will be able to give us the query only next quarter since he is busy with some other work right now_). We store this data in a in-memory cache. This data will then be exposed by multiple endpoints in the provider portal backend. 


