Hi [~accountid:60cdaa45a17463007061ed8e],

Please see below the external counsel’s assessment on the competition law implications: 

{color:#36b37e} _Assuming that Bolt’s market share in Portugal is 30%, the clause in question is not likely to raise serious competition concerns of the kind that companies holding market shares above 30% may rise when requesting similar clauses from their business partners._ {color}

{color:#36b37e}_Without prejudice, we would advise that the temporal scope of the clause does not exceed 3 years which is the period of time usually accepted by the European Commission for the justification of clauses that are formally restrictive._ {color}

{color:#36b37e}_We would also advise that a recital at the beginning of the contract or a paragraph in the clause itself is introduced rendering explicit that the exclusivity is agreed upon considering the investment that Bolt will make in the commercial relationship._ {color}

{color:#36b37e}_If the clause is deemed restrictive of competition, the sanction is both civil (nullity) and punitive (fine up to 10% of annual turnover). In the latter case, however, the application of a fine would require the Competition Authority to make a finding of either: a) dominance in the market by Bolt and consider the clause an abuse of dominant position or b) an agreement between Bolt and the commercial partner with the purpose of harming a third party. None of the possibilities seems straightforward in terms of the construction of a case._ {color}

Following the external counsel’s advice, the wording of the exclusivity clause should be as follows: 

_Considering the investment that Bolt shall make in the business relationship, during the entire period of this Agreement, but for no more than 3 years after the conclusion of the Agreement, the Partner agrees that it will not conclude any agreements for delivery through an online marketplace or any agreements with similar effect or otherwise cooperate with any of Bolt’s competitors in the delivery business. If the Partner breaches this exclusivity clause, the Partner shall pay a penalty in an amount equivalent to [percentage what we want to get for the breach]% of the gross Meal Price of the Orders of the whole Agreement period or [6/12] months preceding the breach (whichever is less) and the Agency Fee payable to Bolt will increase to [new Agency Fee percentage]% as of the date Bolt notifies the Partner of the breach._  

 

Should you have any further questions, please do let me know. 

Many thanks,

