Found out that in case of basket size campaigns, when loading a basket from the db, we don’t apply the campaign on the provider price, but we do apply the campaign on the individual basket items. When updating or removing a basket item we end up subtracting a discounted price from an original price. This is caught in the PriceModel constructor and fallbacks to the original price, while also adding a log. As a result it does not break the business, but it should be fixed.

{noformat}BasketModel#updateBasketItem {
  provider_price: { value: 15.15, original_value: 15.15 },
  basket_item_total_price: { value: 12.12, original_value: 15.15 },
  new_basket_item_total_price: { value: 11.76, original_value: 14.7 }
}{noformat}


